    "['no shutdown', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, Juniper also commonly uses the following format:\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 disable false\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper uses `ge` instead of `GigabitEthernet` for interface naming\\n2. `no shutdown` in Cisco becomes `disable false` in Juniper (or simply omitted, as interfaces are enabled by default in Juniper)\\n3. The `unit 0` is often required in Juniper configurations for logical interfaces', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 disable false', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, Juniper also commonly uses the following format:\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 disable false\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper uses `ge` instead of `GigabitEthernet` for interface naming\\n2. `no shutdown` in Cisco becomes `disable false` in Juniper (or simply omitted, as interfaces are enabled by default in Juniper)\\n3. The `unit 0` is often required in Juniper configurations for logical interfaces', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 disable false'}]]": 1,
